From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:09:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the DSU operating points

Add the operating points of the DSU, and the dsu node that uses them, in
a file of their own, which a board includes with the DSU supply, as it
does the CPU operating points.

The speed bin picks the points and voltages as in the CPU tables:
opp-supported-hw has bit b set for fuse value b, and
opp-microvolt-speed<b> holds the voltage of that bin. Bit 0 and the
unnamed opp-microvolt are the worst-case set: the highest voltage of any
bin, on the points that every bin runs. Every voltage has the 1.05 V
ceiling of the CPU rails as maximum, so that the DSU and the A55 cluster
share one window on their regulator. Only bins 4 and 5 are run on our
boards; the other columns are vendor values, marked so in the file.

Based on the DSU table of the Allwinner BSP device tree, 26 MHz column
family. Differences: the column for a zero fuse is not carried, as a
zero fuse and bin 0 cannot be told apart, and with it the three points
only that column lists; the worst-case set is added; fuse values 0x11
and 0x12, which have no DSU column, get the worst case.

Not covered: the clock latency of the vendor table, which the DSU
governor does not use.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the DSU takes the
points of its speed bin (bin 4 on one board, bin 5 on the other), a
forced highest point sets DCDC5 to the voltage of the bin's column, and
the worst-case set is not used.

Assisted-by: LLM
